.TH TTZIP 1 "2026-08-24" "1.0.0" "TTZip User Manual"
.SH NAME
ttzip \- ultra-high-performance native archiving, extraction, and compression engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ttzip
[\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.br
.B ttzip create
[\fB\-l\fR \fILEVEL\fR] [\fB\-p\fR \fIPASSWORD\fR] [\fB\-s\fR \fISPLIT_SIZE\fR] \fIARCHIVE\fR \fISOURCES...\fR
.br
.B ttzip extract
[\fB\-o\fR \fIDESTINATION\fR] [\fB\-p\fR \fIPASSWORD\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-force\fR] \fIARCHIVE\fR
.br
.B ttzip list
[\fB\-p\fR \fIPASSWORD\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] \fIARCHIVE\fR
.br
.B ttzip inspect
[\fB\-p\fR \fIPASSWORD\fR] \fIARCHIVE\fR
.br
.B ttzip test
[\fB\-p\fR \fIPASSWORD\fR] \fIARCHIVE\fR
.br
.B ttzip bench
[\fBmatrix\fR|\fBgate\fR|\fBdeflate\fR|\fBzstd\fR|\fBsnappy\fR]
.br
.B ttzip salvage
[\fB\-o\fR \fIDESTINATION\fR] \fICORRUPTED_ARCHIVE\fR
.br
.B ttzip doctor
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBTTZip\fR is an ultra-high-performance archiving engine engineered with a pure Safe Rust microkernel and SOTA dual-ISA vector acceleration (ARM64 NEON/PMULL and x86_64 AVX2/CLMUL).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBcreate\fR \fIARCHIVE\fR \fISOURCES...\fR
Compress and pack specified source files or directories into the target archive.
.TP
\fBextract\fR \fIARCHIVE\fR [\fB\-o\fR \fIDESTINATION\fR]
Extract an archive into the specified destination directory with ZipSlip security protection and APFS preallocation.
.TP
\fBlist\fR \fIARCHIVE\fR
List entries in the archive with uncompressed sizes, compressed ratios, and modification timestamps.
.TP
\fBinspect\fR \fIARCHIVE\fR
Perform deep structural inspection and metadata compliance analysis of archive headers.
.TP
\fBtest\fR \fIARCHIVE\fR
Verify archive cryptographic integrity, CRC32/CRC64 checksums, and Reed-Solomon parity records without writing to disk.
.TP
\fBbench\fR [\fBmatrix\fR|\fBgate\fR]
Run hardware SIMD micro-benchmarks and verify 50-point SOTA codec matrix throughput.
.TP
\fBsalvage\fR \fICORRUPTED_ARCHIVE\fR
Attempt deep memory-mapped reconstruction and salvage readable file payloads from damaged archives.
.TP
\fBdoctor\fR
Inspect host CPU capabilities, hardware vector extensions, and memory subsystem topology.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-level\fR \fILEVEL\fR
Compression level: 0 (Store), 1 (Fastest), 3 (Fast), 6 (Normal), 9 (Maximum), 12 (Ultra).
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-password\fR \fIPASSWORD\fR
Specify password for WinZip AES-256 or ZipCrypto encryption/decryption.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIDESTINATION\fR
Destination directory for extraction or output path.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite existing destination files without prompting.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-split\fR \fISIZE\fR
Split output archive into volumes of specified size (e.g. 100M, 1G, 700M).
